  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A brief practice sequence is available after the rules explanation, and the components can be reset before the actual game.\", \"decision\": \"How should players try unfamiliar actions before scored play?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nPlayers who want practice take a short unscored sequence with the teacher while others watch, then the table resets. Additional rehearsal follows expressed need while all players can observe the same examples before scored play.\nThe teacher plays a brief practice sequence while players suggest actions, then resets the components for the game. The group can test its understanding collaboratively without putting any individual player on the spot.\nEach player tries one unfamiliar action during a brief practice sequence before the table resets the components. Everyone has a chance to connect the explanation to a physical turn before choices begin to count."
    }
  ],
